  "onboardingPrivacyEyebrow": "Privacy",
  "onboardingPrivacyTitle": "Your reading stays yours",
  "onboardingPrivacyBody": "OpenPages has no account and no servers that collect your data. Your books and notes never leave this device.",
  "onboardingPrivacyLocal": "Stored only on this device",
  "onboardingPrivacyLocalCaption": "Books, highlights, notes and progress",
  "onboardingPrivacyTracking": "No ads, analytics or tracking",
  "onboardingPrivacyTrackingCaption": "OpenPages doesn't know what you read",
  "onboardingPrivacyLookup": "Only looked-up words go online",
  "onboardingPrivacyLookupCaption": "Turn online lookups off any time in Settings",
  "onboardingImport": "Import your first book",
  "onboardingExplore": "Explore first",
  "onboardingAgreementPrefix": "By continuing, you agree to the ",
  "onboardingAgreementMiddle": " and acknowledge the ",
  "onboardingAgreementSuffix": ".",
  "privacyIntro": "OpenPages is a reader for books and documents you already own. This policy explains what happens to your information when you use it. The short version: your library stays on your device, and we don't collect anything about you.",
  "privacyCollectTitle": "What we collect",
  "privacyCollectBody": "Nothing. OpenPages has no account or sign-in, and no servers of ours receive your books, notes, reading habits or any personal information. We can't see, sell or share what we never receive.",
  "privacyDeviceTitle": "What stays on your device",
  "privacyDeviceBody": "Your books, highlights, notes, bookmarks, saved words, reading progress and settings are stored in the app's private storage on this device. Other apps can't read them, and there is no cloud sync.\n\nUninstalling OpenPages deletes all of this data. Export a backup first if you want to keep it.",
  "privacyLookupTitle": "Word lookups",
  "privacyLookupBody": "When you look up a word, only that single word is sent to dictionaryapi.dev, a free public dictionary service, to fetch its definition. The surrounding text, the book's title and anything else you read stay on the device. Definitions are saved locally, so each word works offline after its first lookup.\n\nIf you choose to open a word on Wiktionary, it opens in your browser under Wiktionary's own privacy policy. You can turn online lookups off, or clear saved definitions, in Settings.",
  "privacyListenTitle": "Read aloud",
  "privacyListenBody": "Read aloud uses the text-to-speech engine installed on your device. OpenPages passes the text being read to that engine and nothing else. Most engines work offline; if yours uses online voices, its provider's privacy policy applies. You can choose or change the engine in your device's settings.",
  "privacyBackupTitle": "Backups",
  "privacyBackupBody": "A backup is created only when you export one from Settings. It is a file containing your book list, annotations and settings, saved wherever you choose. OpenPages never uploads it. Anyone with access to the file can read its contents, so store it somewhere you trust.",
  "privacyPurchasesTitle": "Purchases",
  "privacyPurchasesBody": "Premium is sold through Google Play. Google handles the payment under its own privacy policy, and your payment details never reach OpenPages. The app only asks Google Play whether you own Premium so it can unlock it.",
  "privacyTrackingTitle": "No ads, analytics or tracking",
  "privacyTrackingBody": "OpenPages contains no advertising, analytics, crash reporting or third-party tracking code. It does not build a profile of you, and it does not know what you read.",
  "privacyPermissionsTitle": "Permissions",
  "privacyPermissionsBody": "OpenPages only opens the files you pick or share with it. It uses the internet for word lookups and for checking purchases with Google Play, and nothing else.",
  "privacyChildrenTitle": "Children",
  "privacyChildrenBody": "OpenPages collects no personal information from anyone, including children. Purchases go through Google Play, where family controls apply.",
  "privacyChangesTitle": "Changes and contact",
  "privacyChangesBody": "If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top. Material changes will be shown in the app before they take effect.\n\nQuestions about privacy? Contact us through the developer contact on the OpenPages Google Play listing.",
  "termsTitle": "Terms of Use",
  "termsIntro": "These terms are the agreement between you and the developer of OpenPages (\"we\", \"us\") for using the app. We've kept them short and in plain language. Please read them together with the Privacy Policy.",
  "termsAgreementTitle": "Agreeing to these terms",
  "termsAgreementBody": "By installing or using OpenPages, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the app. Using OpenPages through Google Play also means Google Play's own terms apply.",
  "termsLicenseTitle": "Your license to use OpenPages",
  "termsLicenseBody": "We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use OpenPages on devices you own or control. The app, its design and its name belong to us and our licensors. Open-source components are covered by their own licenses, listed in Settings.",
  "termsContentTitle": "Your books and files",
  "termsContentBody": "You choose what to open in OpenPages, and you're responsible for having the right to read it. OpenPages is made for DRM-free content and doesn't remove or bypass copy protection.\n\nYour content stays yours. We claim no rights to anything you import, highlight or write, and we never receive it.",
  "termsPremiumTitle": "Premium",
  "termsPremiumBody": "OpenPages is free to use. Premium adds optional extras and is offered as a yearly subscription or a one-time lifetime purchase, at the price shown in the app before you buy.\n\nPayments are processed by Google Play. A subscription renews automatically each year until you cancel it in Google Play; cancelling stops the next renewal, and Premium stays active until the end of the period you've paid for. Refunds are handled by Google Play under its refund policy. We may improve or change Premium features over time, but we won't take away what a lifetime purchase unlocked.",
  "termsThirdPartyTitle": "Third-party services",
  "termsThirdPartyBody": "Some features rely on services we don't run: dictionaryapi.dev for definitions, Wiktionary when you open a word there, your device's text-to-speech engine, and Google Play for purchases. Each is governed by its own terms. Definitions come from public sources and may be incomplete or inaccurate.",
  "termsUseTitle": "Fair use",
  "termsUseBody": "Please don't use OpenPages to break the law or infringe anyone's rights, and don't copy, resell, or reverse engineer the app except where the law allows it.",
  "termsWarrantyTitle": "No warranty",
  "termsWarrantyBody": "We work hard to make OpenPages reliable, but it is provided \"as is\" and \"as available\", without warranties of any kind, to the extent the law allows. Your library lives only on your device, so we recommend exporting backups regularly.",
  "termsLiabilityTitle": "Limitation of liability",
  "termsLiabilityBody": "To the extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential losses, or for lost data, arising from your use of OpenPages. Our total liability is limited to the amount you paid for Premium in the twelve months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer protection law that can't be waived.",
  "termsChangesTitle": "Changes and ending",
  "termsChangesBody": "We may update these terms as the app evolves. We'll change the date at the top and show material changes in the app; continuing to use OpenPages afterwards means you accept them. You can stop using OpenPages at any time by uninstalling it.",
  "termsContactTitle": "Contact",
  "termsContactBody": "Questions about these terms? Contact us through the developer contact on the OpenPages Google Play listing.",
